{#
    VIP — a private front door: /vip/{slug}

    Jon makes an entry here for someone, writes a private note on them in
    `jonsonSummary`, and sends them this URL — or its code form, /vip/{altSlug},
    minted on first save (see modules/jonson/services/Vip). Landing on either
    doesn't render a page: it remembers who they are (a signed cookie holding the
    entry's uid) and sends them to the homepage, where Jonson is primed with the
    note for the whole visit and every page carries a small strip saying VIP +
    their name.

    An entry with no note isn't a door: nothing is remembered and the visitor
    arrives home as anyone else. Disabling the entry revokes the door for everyone
    who already holds its cookie. The code URL is handled by controllers/
    VipController; both end in Vip::enter(), so they can't drift apart.
#}
{% do craft.app.getModule('jonson').vip.enter(entry) %}
{% exit %}
